    "text": "To determine the total time Tony spent solving puzzles, we need to break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Time spent on the warm-up puzzle:**\n   Tony spent 10 minutes on the warm-up puzzle.\n\n2. **Time spent on the first puzzle:**\n   The first puzzle took 3 times as long as the warm-up puzzle. Therefore, the time spent on the first puzzle is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 10 = 30 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Time spent on the second puzzle:**\n   The second puzzle also took 3 times as long as the warm-up puzzle. Therefore, the time spent on the second puzzle is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 10 = 30 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total time spent solving puzzles:**\n   To find the total time spent, we add the time spent on the warm-up puzzle, the first puzzle, and the second puzzle:\n   \\[\n   10 + 30 + 30 = 70 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total time Tony spent solving puzzles is \\(\\boxed{70}\\) minutes.",
